EDGSRC=../../../external/edg/src

# cpfe -- EDG's C++ front end, built from EDG's own C.  One binary from
# 75 translation units; `src/cfe.c' is the only one with a `main'.
# See sys/src/external/edg/NOTE for how the C was produced and for the
# target configuration, `kencc_targ.h', which is committed beside it.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT IN `sys/src/cmd/mkfile''s app lists, and the reason
# is this tree's own: ONE FAILING ENTRY ABORTS THE WHOLE TREE'S `mk',
# which is why `basic' and `c++lib' are commented out there too.  Build
# this directory BY HAND until it comes back clean.
#
# TWO THINGS ARE EXPECTED TO BE MEASURED HERE, in this order, and they
# are different questions with different answers.
#
# 1. DOES pcc COMPILE IT.  Nothing in this directory has ever been
#    through pcc.  `src/sys_predef.c' is **315,616 lines in one
#    translation unit** (`ifc_modules_read.c' is 130,330 and
#    `expr.c' 120,824), so a compiler table limit is the first thing
#    likely to answer, and it would be kencc's answer rather than the
#    port's -- worth knowing before anything is blamed on EDG.
#    **RUN IT AS `mk -k'.** Plan 9 mk stops at the first failing
#    recipe, so a plain `mk' costs one round per bad file across 75
#    files; -k compiles the rest and the run names every one at once.
#    That is the rule this tree has paid for twice -- bacon's missing
#    header names and bacon's missing link symbols were both asked all
#    at once rather than one per round, and both came back complete.
#
# 2. THEN THE LINK, WHICH IS THE KNOWN WALL.  `mkone' compiles every
#    OFILE before it links, so a compile pass followed by a link
#    failure is the expected shape and is TWO results rather than one.
#    EDG emulates COMDAT for vague linkage -- inline functions,
#    template instantiations, vtables, typeinfo -- and with the kencc
#    target that emulation emits no `__weak__' at all (38,245 applied
#    attributes went to 0), so the duplicates are now plain. Measured
#    on two trivial translation units sharing one header: they collide
#    on **10 symbols**; across these 75 files **3,094 COMDAT symbols
#    are named in more than one**.  `6l' will say which, and its list
#    is worth more than that grep -- the grep counts annotations, some
#    of which are declarations rather than definitions, so 3,094 is an
#    UPPER bound on colliding definitions.
#    Neither answer to that is reached by editing this mkfile:
#    `--one_instantiation_per_object' covers only the template share
#    (3 of the 10) and makes the output depend on an `edg_prelink'
#    phase, and upstream's answer for a target without COMDAT is the
#    Cfront-like ABI, which was attempted and backed out.  The NOTE
#    carries both and where each stops.
#
# NO -I AND NO -D: each file declares everything it uses, including its
# own `void *memcpy(void *, const void *, unsigned long long)', where
# the `unsigned long long' is kencc's size_t from `kencc_targ.h'.
# CFLAGS is `-c' alone so that nothing is quieted on the first run.
#
# `LIB=' IS ANSWERED, AND cpfe NEEDS EXACTLY ONE SYMBOL FROM libedg.a.
# This was left as a question here -- "only the link says which are
# undefined" -- on the grounds that `src' holds 145,752 distinct
# `_Z'-prefixed tokens and a grep over them measures nothing.  That is
# still true of a grep; it is not true of the LINKER'S OWN ANSWER,
# which can be had on the host without a VM: compile all 133 files with
# gcc, take `nm -u' over `src''s 75 objects, and subtract both what
# those objects define and what `lib_src''s 51 define.
#
#	src/ externals                               629
#	  satisfied by libedg.a                        1   `_ZnwyPv'
#	  plain C names, all present in libap         70
#	  gcc artefacts, absent under pcc              2
#	  template instantiations, defined NOWHERE   556
#
# The one is `_ZnwyPv' -- `operator new(unsigned long long, void *)',
# PLACEMENT new -- from `lib_src/placenew.c'.  So the line below is
# needed and it is needed for one small member, which is also why
# lib/edg must be built first: in `mkone' `$LIB' is a PREREQUISITE of
# `$O.out' handed straight to `$LD', the dependency that had `bacon'
# unbuildable until lua was.
#
# *A host measurement, with the caveat said rather than left out*: it
# measures the NAMES in the C, which pcc and gcc must agree on because
# the C is the same text.  What it cannot speak for is whether `6l'
# reports the same SET -- an archive is pulled member by member, so the
# order and the reachability are the linker's.
#
# THE PREDICTION FOR THE FIRST LINK, written before it is run: `6l'
# reports undefined `_ZN3edg...I...E' names and nothing else -- around
# 556 of them, every one a TEMPLATE INSTANTIATION that no translation
# unit emitted.  Zero vtables, zero typeinfo, zero guard variables,
# zero thunks; those are all on the DUPLICATE side of the problem
# (3,124 symbols defined in more than one object), not this one.  If
# `6l' instead names a plain C function, or a vtable, the instantiation
# reading is wrong and the NOTE's link-model section needs re-reading
# rather than this mkfile.
#
# `-C' IS WHY THIS LINKS AT ALL, AND IT IS IN CFLAGS ABOVE.  The first
# link reported `redefinition:' until `too many errors' -- NOT the
# undefined names predicted here, because `6l' catches duplicates as it
# LOADS each object and only reports undefined symbols at the end, so
# it never reached the pass that prediction was about.  The symbols it
# named are the ones the host sweep had already measured:
# `edg::max_val<unsigned long long>' and `edg::skip_typerefs', both at
# 41 copies, and `Ptr_map<...>::get_with_hash' at 39.
#
# `-C' marks every TEXT and GLOBL in the translation unit `dupok', so
# `6l' keeps the first definition and discards the rest -- COMDAT,
# which it has implemented since forever behind a bit nothing in C
# could set.  The full account is in `cc/cc.h'.  It is blunt (every
# symbol, not just the vague-linkage ones) and that is safe HERE and
# only here, because every duplicate in generated C is the same entity
# by construction.  Nothing else in the tree passes it.
#
# And the fix for that is NOT here: it is an instantiation-mode flag at
# the next TRANSLATION, so cpfe emits the definitions.  The NOTE says
# why `--one_instantiation_per_object' is the wrong lever -- it covers
# only part of the set and makes the output depend on an `edg_prelink'
# phase that mk cannot naturally express.
#
# One thing the runtime does NOT do, checked rather than assumed,
# because this tree has paid for it once: it adds nothing libap
# already provides.  Every DEFINITION under `lib_src' is `_Z'-mangled
# or `__'-prefixed -- `exit.c' defines `_Z4exiti', `memzero.c' defines
# `__memzero' -- and the plain C names (`memset', `memcpy', `malloc',
# `free', `abort', `exit') appear only as DECLARATIONS, so they resolve
# to libap rather than replacing it.  *The filenames read alarmingly
# and the definitions do not*, which is the declaration/definition
# distinction the `reject' round cost a build over.

